<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Michiel de Ruyter</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1607–1676</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Michiel Adriaenszoon de Ruyter</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Michiel de Ruyter was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> admiral, the most celebrated commander of the Dutch navy. During the Second and Third <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-dutch-wars">Anglo-Dutch Wars</a> he won the Four Days' Battle in 1666, led the Raid on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-medway">Medway</a> in 1667, when the English flagship Royal Charles was towed away, and fought off the combined English and French fleets in 1672–1673. He died of wounds received in battle against the French off <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> in 1676.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/michiel-de-ruyter.jpg" alt="Michiel de Ruyter" width="320" height="368" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ferdinand Bol · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bol,_Michiel_de_Ruyter.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
